> However if I use beta the model performs and converges poorly, my impression is that the beta

*Gamma (not beta)

> is harder to model, because of its wide spectra of shapes it can acquire.
>
> For example the convergence modeling standard deviation as normal is much stable (even though does not interpret the data well).
>
> Now:
>
> 1) which density function can I use that would be more contrained, or
> 2) does it make sense to fix a parameter of the beta, or

*Gamma (not beta)

> 3) in what other way can I model the standard deviation/variance?
>
> Thanks.
