Thanks for this Bob. You're right, I should have left the variables names the same to begin with.

I think, however, that because in Bugs the scale parameter in normal() is the precision, it should instead be the following in the likelihood:

1 / sqrt(tauj[j] * taui[i])

And I think there also needs to be normal(0, 1) priors on the _raws:

zhat1_raw ~ normal(0, 1);
zhat2_raw ~ normal(0, 1);

Is that right?

Regarding the Bugs model itself, I'm curious if it will fit with diffuse inits. The authors included the same random inits for both of their chains. I'll have to test that to see if it's the model itself, which would be unfortunate.

