Why do I want all this (I'll use Roman/Greek notation):

When get mu[1], mu[2], and mu[3] from

y[n] ~ normal(a[n,1] * mu[1] + a[n,2] * mu[2] + a[n,3] * mu[3], sigma)

And give it to a biologist, I get the question can you tell me if mu[1], mu[2], and mu[3] are significantly different.

I have the feeling that in a Bayesian context this question could not make much sense, although this paper deal with this problem (http://www.indiana.edu/~kruschke/BEST/BEST.pdf <http://www.indiana.edu/%7Ekruschke/BEST/BEST.pdf>).

