Hi Daniel,

you got it the less multiplication by factor 2 was the idea to write
a triangular matrix function.

I think going the road with the eigenvectors/eigenvalues instead
of the cholesky decomposition is a more promising one.

http://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/61719/cholesky-versus-eigendecomposition-for-drawing-samples-from-a-multivariate-norma

The scaling of eta and sigma noise of the GP leads to just a translation and scaling of the eigenvalues.

Andre

