Awesome. That does sound hopeful.

Before you get to that point, check the stepsizes. Make sure they're all the same order of magnitude. Then check to see that the tree depth is consistently a low number. If you're able to achieve both, my guess is that your n_eff per unit time will be an order of magnitude greater.

Daniel

